/** Plain-English evidence for l20, generated from completed run records. */
import {writeFile} from 'node:fs/promises';import {ROOT,json,rec,num,array} from './inputs.mts';import {L20} from './gaia-old.mts';
import {readBarGeometry,projectedBar} from './bar-geometry.mts';import {bodyToSky} from './geometry.mts';
const f=(v:unknown,n=4)=>num(v).toFixed(n),pct=(a:unknown,b:unknown)=>100*(num(a)/num(b)-1);
const small=rec(await json(L20+'result.json')),tiny=rec(await json(L20+'tiny/result.json')),before=rec(await json(L20+'../l18/result.json')),a=rec(before.residuals),b=rec(small.residuals),colors=rec(await json(L20+'bar-color.json')),p=rec(colors.photo),c=rec(colors.l20),d=rec(colors.l18),texture=rec(await json(L20+'bar-contrast.json')),tp=rec(texture.photo),ta=rec(texture.l18),tb=rec(texture.l20),model=rec(await json(L20+'old-population.json')),old=rec(model.oldSelection),controls=rec(small.sceneControls),vmc=rec(model.vmcCheck),bar=rec(model.barMeasured);
const colorPassed=Math.abs(pct(c.rg,p.rg))<=2&&Math.abs(pct(c.bg,p.bg))<=2,rmsPassed=pct(b.trainRelativeRms,a.trainRelativeRms)<=1&&pct(b.heldoutRelativeRms,a.heldoutRelativeRms)<=1,contrastPassed=texture.powerCloser===true,tinyPassed=rec(tiny.fit).rmsPassed===true;
const geometry=readBarGeometry(model.publishedShapeCheck),reference=projectedBar(geometry),center=bodyToSky(geometry.center);await writeFile(L20+'shape-check.json',JSON.stringify({gaia:bar,publishedConstruction:{...reference,skyCenterWestNorthKpc:center.slice(0,2),intrinsicAxisRatio:geometry.ratio},comparison:'Kacharov/Rathore retained l18 construction versus moments of the Gaia central-excess field. Estimators and tracer weights differ. These are checks, not imposed shapes, and no shift or rotation was fitted.'},null,2)+'\n');
await writeFile(L20+'notes.md',`# l20: measured old stars and stellar grain\n\nThis is a rejected diagnostic; l18 remains retained. The tiny gate failed after three rounds. The requested 512 px images do not overturn that failure.\n\nThe old disc and bar now follow Gaia DR3 red-giant and red-clump density weighted by measured G flux, smoothed with a 100 pc Gaussian sigma. Resolved Gaia old and young stars supply individual positions, fluxes and colors. Their light replaces a share of the unresolved field. Molecular oval screens are removed; their attenuation budget is carried by the HERITAGE layer normalized to Bell.\n\n| Masked bar color | Photo | l18 | l20 | l20 error |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| R/G | ${f(p.rg)} | ${f(d.rg)} | ${f(c.rg)} | ${pct(c.rg,p.rg).toFixed(2)}% |\n| B/G | ${f(p.bg)} | ${f(d.bg)} | ${f(c.bg)} | ${pct(c.bg,p.bg).toFixed(2)}% |\n\n| Check | l18 | l20 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Training RGB relative RMS | ${f(a.trainRelativeRms,6)} | ${f(b.trainRelativeRms,6)} (+${pct(b.trainRelativeRms,a.trainRelativeRms).toFixed(2)}%) |\n| Held-out RGB relative RMS | ${f(a.heldoutRelativeRms,6)} | ${f(b.heldoutRelativeRms,6)} (+${pct(b.heldoutRelativeRms,a.heldoutRelativeRms).toFixed(2)}%) |\n| Masked 2–5 arcmin contrast power | ${f(ta.power,7)} | ${f(tb.power,7)} |\n\nPhoto contrast power is ${f(tp.power,7)}. The color test ${colorPassed?'passes':'fails'} its 2% tolerance, the RMS test ${rmsPassed?'passes':'fails'} its 1% relative regression limit, and contrast ${contrastPassed?'moves closer to the photo':'does not move closer to the photo'}. The contrast-power error is ${(100*(1-num(texture.powerErrorAfter)/num(texture.powerErrorBefore))).toFixed(1)}% smaller than l18, although l20 overshoots the photo power by ${pct(tb.power,tp.power).toFixed(1)}%. The side views remain coherent.\n\nThe remaining issue is spatial: the bar is too broad, and the outer annulus is ${f(array(b.annularDifferencePercent)[3],1)}% too bright. Crowding completeness and the adopted disc/bar partition remain unresolved.\n\nTiny took ${f(tiny.seconds,1)} seconds and small took ${f(small.seconds,1)} seconds, excluding catalogue preparation, archive acquisition and close-up diagnostics. No full fit or slab bake ran. l18 remains available unchanged.\n`);
await writeFile(L20+'method.md',`# l20 method and limits\n\n## Measured old light\n\n[Luri et al. 2021](https://arxiv.org/html/2012.01771), section 2.3.1, supplies the RGB and red-clump CMD polygons. The same published conditional proper-motion selection used for l13 is retained, with signed parallax/error below five and a 99% motion ellipse. Gaia DR3 replaces EDR3. A uniform random-index sample supplies ${old.densityStars} old members; the bright catalogue contains ${old.resolvedOldStars} selected old members with G below 18. Queries cover a 20-degree cone. A truncated single bright-star query was rejected and replaced by complete disjoint magnitude partitions.\n\nThe equal-count first trial failed. The final field weights the selected catalogue by measured G flux, using every bright star with G below 18 and expanding the faint uniform sample by 18.11709771 (the DR3 source count divided by the random-index threshold). This is a luminosity-density tracer, rather than an equal-count density. No photo value sets those weights.\n\nThese measurements are deprojected through the accepted Choi plane and Oden warp, smoothed with a 100 pc Gaussian sigma, then normalized to unit area. The model tapers from 8.5 to 9 kpc, as the retained Gaia young field does. A radial median defines the disc; its positive central excess, tapered between 3 and 4 kpc, defines the bar. Their sum is the measured luminosity-density map in every cell. This partition is adopted, not a published decomposition. No analytic Gaussian supplies old emission. All radii of the measured disc share one old-population RGB grade; the previous analytic outskirts template is absent, so its old scalar has no effect in this replacement.\n\nThe same paper warns that old-population counts are incomplete in the crowded bar (section 7.1 and Figure 18). VMC is a check here, not a correction field. This source limitation remains unresolved.\n\nThe measured central-excess sky PA is ${f(bar.paDegrees,2)} degrees, its projected axis ratio is ${f(bar.axisRatio,3)}, and its major-axis sigma is ${f(bar.sigmaMajorKpc,3)} kpc. The sky centroid in west/north kpc is ${array(bar.skyCenterWestNorthKpc).map(v=>f(v,3)).join(', ')}. [Kacharov](https://arxiv.org/html/2410.05374) and [Rathore](https://arxiv.org/html/2410.18182) remain comparison checks. The retained published construction projects to a ${f(reference.paDegrees,2)}-degree PA, ${f(reference.sigmaMajorKpc,3)} kpc major sigma and ${f(reference.axisRatio,3)} axis ratio, with west/north center ${center.slice(0,2).map(v=>f(v,3)).join(', ')} kpc. The Gaia central-excess field remains broader and more displaced. These differences were not fitted away; they are not imposed on the count field. These are selection-dependent moments, not a new measurement of the published bar parameters. The fixed l18 aperture still defines the color and contrast tests.\n\n[VMC regional counts, Mazzi et al. 2021](https://arxiv.org/html/2108.07225), are checked over ${vmc.regions} footprints. The Pearson correlation is ${f(vmc.correlation,3)}. These are different magnitude and population selections; VMC does not change the Gaia field. Gaia crowding, extinction, magnitude limits and the finite random sample still bias the counts. All-sky coverage does not imply uniform completeness.\n\n## Finite stellar points\n\nThe model contains ${model.points} retained old and young Gaia points. Gaussian height sigmas are adopted and fixed: old disc 410 pc, bar 367 pc, young 150 pc. Each point is placed on its measured sky ray at a deterministic draw from that layer above the warped plane. Individual stellar distances are conditional. The maximum plane/height residual is ${f(model.heightResidualMaxKpc,6)} kpc.\n\n[ESA DR3 photometry](https://gea.esac.esa.int/archive/documentation/GDR3/Data_processing/chap_cu5pho/cu5pho_sec_photProc/cu5pho_ssec_photCal.html) supplies the Vega-to-AB zero-point differences: G +0.1136, BP +0.0155 and RP +0.3561 mag. RP/G/BP mean flux-density ratios serve as broad RGB proxies. The bandpasses differ from the photograph; one global grade per population calibrates that response. Stellar colors are never fitted individually. The adopted dust column conditionally corrects each point before the renderer attenuates it.\n\nOld resolved light is ${(100*num(controls.oldResolvedFraction)).toFixed(2)}% of its population budget; young resolved light is ${(100*num(controls.youngResolvedFraction)).toFixed(2)}%. Positive bounds are 1–40% and 0.5–25%. Unresolved plus point intrinsic G light is conserved for every fraction. Six old/bar RGB coefficients and these two fractions are the only free controls. Catalogue object amplitudes, young/gas grades and the display curve stay at l18.\n\n## Dust and checks\n\nThe l19 HERITAGE fine modulation is used inside the same 250 pc warped layer, with strength 1.025 bounded to 0.25–2. The diffuse field is globally rescaled to Bell's full column budget. Molecular oval geometry no longer attenuates separately and no molecular oval raster is injected. This redistributes their column budget; it does not claim that Herschel determines their depth. Unknown Herschel pixels retain the parent coarse field.\n\nThe photo supplies no stellar density, stellar position or individual stellar color. Existing object-local H-alpha/photo shapes from l18 remain unchanged. Bar color is measured with the same catalogue-masked aperture as l18. Contrast uses mask-normalized log-luminance power between two- and five-arcminute Gaussian FWHM scales, on the same 512-pixel bar crop and 15 pc ray steps as l19. Geometry is never fitted to the photo.\n`);
